 dimensional conformal field theory with a three dimensional boundary, this sum rule in turn relates the two boundary contributions to the anomaly in the trace of the stress tensor. We check our sum rule for a variety of free theories and also for a weakly interacting theory, where a free scalar in the bulk couples marginally to a generalized free field on the boundary.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"Springer"}},{"source":"arXiv","value":"In the context of boundary conformal field theory, we derive a sum rule that relates two and three point functions of the displacement operator. For four dimensional conformal field theory with a three dimensional boundary, this sum rule in turn relates the two boundary contributions to the anomaly in the trace of the stress tensor. We check our sum rule for a variety of free theories and also for a weakly interacting theory, where a free scalar in the bulk couples marginally to a generalized free field on the boundary.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"control_number":1892492,"dois":[{"source":"Springer","value":"10.1007/JHEP01(2022)121"},{"material":"publication","source":"arXiv","value":"10.1007/JHEP01(2022)121"}],"preprint_date":"2021-07-24","arxiv_eprints":[{"categories":["hep-th"],"value":"2107.11604"}],"titles":[{"source":"Springer","title":"A sum rule for boundary contributions to the trace anomaly"},{"source":"arXiv","title":"A Sum Rule for Boundary Contributions to the Trace Anomaly"}],"document_type":["article"]},"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1892492?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1892492?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1892492?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1892492?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1892492?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1892492?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?